    {
      "title": "TLS Mental Model and Handshake",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TLS Mental Model and Handshake",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Guarantees",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Confidentiality==: encryption",
                "==Integrity==: tamper detection",
                "==Authentication==: server proves identity via its certificate"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handshake and Keys",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "ClientHello",
                    "sub": "versions, ciphers, key share",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ServerHello",
                    "sub": "+ certificate + Finished",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Client Finished",
                    "sub": "data flows",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "TLS 1.3 costs ==1 round trip==",
                "Key exchange is ephemeral **ECDHE**: ==forward secrecy==",
                "A stolen server key cannot decrypt past recorded sessions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Job",
                "Speed"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Asymmetric",
                  "authenticate, agree on key",
                  "slow"
                ],
                [
                  "Symmetric (`AES-GCM`, `ChaCha20`)",
                  "==bulk data==",
                  "fast"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Walk through the handshake?** Hello with key share, server hello + cert + Finished, client Finished.",
                "**Forward secrecy?** Per-session keys, so a later key theft reveals no old traffic.",
                "**Why not encrypt all data with the public key?** Too slow; it only authenticates and agrees on a key.",
                "**1.3 removes vs 1.2?** RSA key exchange, weak ciphers, extra round trip."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Asymmetric crypto sets up the key; ==symmetric== encrypts the data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Certificates and HSTS",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Certificates and HSTS",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Chain of Trust",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Leaf",
                    "sub": "key + SAN",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Intermediate",
                    "sub": "signed by root",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Trusted root",
                    "sub": "in OS store",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "X.509 binds a ==public key== to a domain (`SAN`), signed by a **CA**",
                "Client checks the {green:chain}, {orange:expiry} and {blue:hostname match}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com",
                "openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com </dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -dates"
              ],
              "note": "x509 reads stdin, so pipe s_client into it"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "notBefore=Jan  1 00:00:00 2026 GMT",
                "notAfter=Apr  1 00:00:00 2026 GMT"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. HSTS",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Browser forces ==HTTPS== and blocks click-through on cert errors",
                "Active only after the {blue:first HTTPS visit}, unless ==preloaded==",
                "First plain HTTP request can be intercepted: {red:SSL stripping}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**How is a chain validated?** Signatures leaf to intermediate to trusted root, plus expiry and hostname.",
                "**HSTS vs a 301?** A 301 still starts on plain HTTP and can be stripped; HSTS skips HTTP and blocks bypass.",
                "**Preload risks?** Hard to undo, and every subdomain must support HTTPS."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Secure Headers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Secure Headers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Response Headers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CSP== limits script, style and frame sources",
                "Main defence against ==XSS impact==",
                "`nosniff` stops MIME sniffing",
                "`Referrer-Policy` limits URL leakage"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'",
                "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff",
                "Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
              ],
              "note": "baseline response headers"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Framing and Cookies",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Blocks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`frame-ancestors 'none'`",
                  "page being framed"
                ],
                [
                  "`X-Frame-Options: DENY`",
                  "framing (older)"
                ],
                [
                  "`Secure`",
                  "cookie over plain HTTP"
                ],
                [
                  "`HttpOnly`",
                  "JS reading the cookie"
                ],
                [
                  "`SameSite=Lax` or `Strict`",
                  "most CSRF"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Check and Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl -I https://example.com"
              ],
              "note": "-I fetches response headers only"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**CSP and 'unsafe-inline'?** CSP blocks injected scripts; inline allowance lets them run again",
                "**Cookie flags?** Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite: stop sniffing, theft and CSRF",
                "**Check headers?** `curl -I`, look for CSP and nosniff"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "CSP with =='unsafe-inline'== in script-src gives up the XSS defence."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Secrets Management and Supply Chain Risks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Secrets Management and Supply Chain Risks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Secrets",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`.env` in ==.gitignore==; scan with `gitleaks` or `trufflehog`",
                "Secret in git history = ==compromised==: **rotate** it",
                "Deleting the commit is {red:not enough}"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Load at runtime: ==Secrets Manager==, Vault, cloud KMS, or injected env vars",
                "==Least privilege==, rotation, short-lived credentials"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Supply Chain Risks",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Risk",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Known CVEs",
                  "Vulnerable dependency version"
                ],
                [
                  "Typosquatting",
                  "Look-alike package name"
                ],
                [
                  "Dependency confusion",
                  "Public package shadows an internal name"
                ],
                [
                  "Install scripts",
                  "Malicious code runs on install"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Defences",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Commit ==lockfiles==, pin versions",
                "`npm ci` installs exactly the lockfile, fails on mismatch",
                "Audit with `npm audit` or Dependabot",
                "Generate an ==SBOM==; verify provenance and signatures"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "npm ci",
                "npm audit"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Key pushed to GitHub?** Revoke and rotate it, then scan history",
                "**Dependency confusion?** A public package shadows an internal name",
                "**Lockfile + npm ci in CI?** Reproducible, pinned installs; no surprise versions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
